  "reason": "RTL registers every pin: inputs land in kept pin flops (quadrant: cw -> 11 kept P1 copies, thr -> 6 kept threshold copies, ties -> 4 kept tie copies, in_line -> in_p1; ctl: cw_r/k_r, a_ret/a_qf), outputs are registers (quadrant: selected_v_o/selected_line_o/ret/qfault_o; ctl: cw, threshold, ties, fault); every edge is in the IDX calendar (registered_s3). A synthesis wrapper would add a second, unpriced stage. clk / rst_n pass through."
 },
 "structural_change": "HBM-IDX6 FAN32 (10-20) successor of hidx_sel_s3c_b: same ports / timing / arithmetic (lockstep-equivalent to the s3 original), every register and combinational net <= 32 actual load pins by replicated state (kept P1 copies per consumer family, per-chunk kept flags, one-edge-ahead one-hot rotate selects from replicated fill state, per-chunk pack prefix copies, regional reset leaves). Predecessor failed the mandatory native32 census (s3q 497 drivers / max 1788; s3c d_go 61, reset leaf 115). L2H-IDXSEL s3 (LEAD3-HBM route B 10-19): the ctl child tile of the landed IDX selector cluster (control-word pin flops, reset landing, choose pipeline on the returned histogram stream, fault); 54.0 x 64.8; S face = die control ports, W/E = the W/E quadrants' landed ret/ties/qf, N = cw/thr rings.",
 "slot_change_request": "new child of the s3 landed cluster (centre column of hidx_sel_s3p)",
